  "slug": "full-roman-numerals",
  "title": "HighTide's Full Roman Numerals",
  "description": "This project is a resource pack that fixes Minecraft's roman numerals so they display properly.",
  "body": "**HighTide's Full Roman Numerals** is a resource pack that fixes the issue where enchantments higher than level 10 will appear as `enchantment.level.11` all the way until `enchantment.level.255`. This happens becuase Mojang didn't expect people to apply higher enchantments, even if we do.\n\nThis resource pack fixes this by replacing enchantment.level.11 - enchantment.level.255 with the actual roman numerals.\n\nHere's some examples:\n<details>\n<summary>Spoiler</summary>\n<ul>\n  <li>Instead of <code>enchantment.level.156</code>, its <code>CLVI</code>.</li>\n  <li>Instead of <code>enchantment.level.148</code>, its <code>CXLVIII</code>.</li>\n  <li>Instead of <code>enchantment.level.238</code>, its <code>CCXXXVIII</code>.</li>\n</ul>\nAnd the list can just keep going...\n</details>\n\nIf Mojang ever decides to increase the enchantment level limit back to 32767, I'll be sure to update this resource pack to have roman numerals all the way up until `ↂↂↂↀↀDCCLXVII` (32767).",
